{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git log -9 --oneline --no-decorate; sed -n '55,88p' docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md; rg -n 'hardening2|hardening-2|reconcil|DENIED|SIGN-OFF|full JVM' orchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"0bf8bc4e merge-resolution: reconcile the yang-clojure track's session logs and ledger after the master rebase\n7723c6ae fix(latte): require executed arities for gate coverage\nad04a284 docs(test): provenance note for the named-integration coverage basis\nd6cc2cc2 test(latte): close residual kernel gate fixtures\na926ee31 test(yang): record the slice-9 gate verification\nef9ddd5d fix(yang.clojure): preserve fresh supply through have steps\n211dded9 fix(yang.clojure): close kernel hardening dependency blockers\n65e326f3 test(yang): the slice-9 kernel differential gate — BLOCKED, recorded honestly\n0dc5d7af fix(docker): split order in assigned-subsystems (env unset → nil → run all)\n\n## Coordination contract\n\nThe orchestrator owns scope, authorization, verification, consensus, and\nreadiness; the Workflow section owns the sequence.\n\n**Commit authority** (2026-10-26 owner ruling). Staging, committing, merging\nto master, and pushing are authorized by exactly one of:\n\n- **An Architect sign-off** ([`architect.md`](architect.md)) on completed\n  work whose step 7 review has finished and whose findings are reconciled.\n  The sign-off covers exactly the signed-off work, never unrelated changes\n  that happen to be in the tree.\n- **An explicit user instruction.** Only the user can waive step 7 review\n  (2026-09-23 owner ruling).\n- **The trivial-edit exemption.** A trivial direct edit as defined in Scope\n  of judgment (a typo fix, a mechanical rename, a doc cross-reference\n  update: no choice between approaches, no behavior change) needs neither\n  review nor sign-off.\n\nLocal verification (step 6) is never a substitute for any of these. History\nrewrites (amend, revert, reset) are outside all three, with one exception: an\nunauthorized pre-review commit that is local, unpushed, and unmerged is\nsoft-reset and the work goes through review, never reviewed after the fact.\nAny other rewrite needs the user.\n\nFor cost constraints and CLI routing caveats, see [`team.md`](../team.md)'s\n**Available Subscriptions & Cost Constraints** table. For current, session-\nindependent owner-relayed availability and budget status (an outage, a\nnarrowed authorization, a near-empty quota), see\n[`routing-status.md`](../routing-status.md) — check it before routing to a\nmetered destination, and add an entry when the owner relays a new status.\n\n## Artifact protocol\n13:Done: Re-read docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md (scope of judgment, coordination contract, commit authority, artifact protocol, Workflow 1-11) per the owner's instruction. Re-derived state from the real tree: master stable at 63674368; this track's three branches are pushed and untouched by the repair — yang-common-call@0a15d053 (adoption fix round: codex 1eb14d06 + kimi 0a15d053), yang-hardening2@4c914c05 (hardening-2 arity correction), yang-slice9@7dc18478 (the BLOCKED kernel gate, preserved deliberately).\n24:Done: (1) All three track branches rebased onto the repaired master (ledger conflicts resolved by the union rule both times: 140 and 130 rows, zero markers) and re-verified: adoption 127/1273 + oracle 21/971; hardening-2 suites 122/1338 with its oracle correctly :blocked (20 unexercised arities — the expected state, not a pass). (2) glm confirmation round (session 346a33f5; note its collab/ writes were DENIED so the report lived only in stdout — extracted to findings): ALL SIX original findings CLOSED with its own re-run probes, eligibility follow-up VERIFIED, plus two new P2s: N1 (yang.call/invoke + invoke-with are native-name? operators that bypass the admission witness — a forged assoc map runs; forged scalar/guest-fn entries surface a raw host defect) and N2 (closure manifests missing call.cljc; dao.host.gate-test red on all three lanes). (3) Escalated N1 to the section architect (kimi r5, session_0cbe7179): ruling = witness-gate both operators at the compile branch like yang.call/eligible?; a ledger deviation would contradict r4(a); no shared-runtime change needed; N2 is mechanical. (4) N1/N2 fix round to kimi -> committed 12feb7d1 (gate both operators, refusal/positive/dynamic-eligibility/non-symbol fixtures, three closure manifests regenerated + gate totals updated, dao.host.gate-test adjustments). Verified this seat: 142/1472 across the five suites incl. dao.host.gate-test, oracle 21/971, kondo clean; ran the two N1 fixtures by name (7 and 16 assertions green).\n35:Done: glm r3 confirmation (session 3e4d9593, resumed after a plan-only stop): N1 CLOSED (all forged shapes refuse with the qualified :yang.call/not-callable via both operators incl. the def-alias route; admitted + dynamic-eligibility intact both lanes), N2 CLOSED (dao.host.gate-test 14/178; manifests 156/154/155, union 168) — \"Ready for Architect sign-off\". astra sign-off r1 DENIED on a real P2 the seat had not caught: the invocation admission gate skipped ARGUMENT evaluation on refusal (§8.10.4 requires operands once, left-to-right, before the callee check) — reproduced on both lanes at 12feb7d1 vs abbfb998. Fix round to kimi -> committed 45269e0f (all operands bound before the witness check, both branches reuse the bindings, refused/admitted regressions both lanes). This seat verified 143/1484 across the five suites + oracle 21/971 + kondo 0 errors. astra SIGN-OFF GRANTED for 63674368..45269e0f, conditions: final-commit shiva Node/Dart lanes + the dao.stream merge gate.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
